.TH MAGENTA 1 "October 31, 2026" "magenta" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
magenta \- manage the rules, colorschemes, and settings of mgnt
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B magenta
.I command
[\fIarguments\fR]
.br
.B magenta
.BR \-\-help | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B magenta
manages what
.BR mgnt (1)
uses to color logs: the rules that tell kinds of input apart and color them, the colorschemes that hold the colors, and the settings in
.IR config.toml .
It never shows logs.
To color a log, use
.BR mgnt (1).
.PP
Files live in the configuration directory, which
.B magenta doctor
prints.
A file of the user with the same name as a built-in one overrides it.
A new name adds a rule or colorscheme.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B magenta colorscheme list
List the colorschemes and where each one comes from.
.TP
.BI "magenta colorscheme show " name
Print a colorscheme file.
.TP
.BI "magenta colorscheme new " name
Create a new colorscheme file from a template.
.TP
.BI "magenta colorscheme edit " name
Edit a colorscheme in
.BR $EDITOR ,
then check it.
.TP
.RI "magenta colorscheme check [" name ]
Check a colorscheme file, or every colorscheme when none is given.
.TP
.BI "magenta colorscheme use " name
Make a colorscheme the one that
.B mgnt
uses.
.TP
.B magenta rule list
.TQ
.BI "magenta rule show " name
.TQ
.BI "magenta rule new " name
.TQ
.BI "magenta rule edit " name
.TQ
.RI "magenta rule check [" name ]
The same five commands for rules.
.TP
.B magenta config get
.TQ
.BI "magenta config get " key
Print one setting, or all of them.
.TP
.BI "magenta config set " "key value"
Change a setting in
.IR config.toml .
.TP
.B magenta config path
Print the path of
.IR config.toml .
.TP
.BI "magenta detect " file
Read the first lines of a file and print how each rule scores against them, and which rule
.B mgnt
would pick.
Use it to tune the detect patterns of a rule.
.TP
.B magenta doctor
Report the configuration, what
.B mgnt
detects, the color depth,
.BR fzf (1),
and how fast
.B mgnt
starts.
Include its output in a bug report.
.TP
.B magenta init
Copy the built-in rules and colorschemes into the configuration directory for editing, and write a
.I config.toml
with the defaults.
Files that already exist are not touched.
.TP
.RB "magenta preview [" "rule " "[" "colorscheme" "]]"
Print the sample lines of a rule, or of every rule, colored with a colorscheme.
.B \-\-theme
chooses the dark or the light palette.
.TP
.BI "magenta completion " shell
Print a completion script for
.BR bash ,
.BR zsh ,
.BR fish ,
or
.BR powershell .
.TP
.BR "magenta help" " [\fIcommand\fR]"
Show the help of a command.
.SH SETTINGS
These keys work with
.B magenta config set
and as
.B mgnt \-\-set
values.
.TP
.B colorscheme
The colorscheme to use.
Default
.BR magenta .
.TP
.B theme
.BR dark ,
.BR light ,
or
.BR auto .
Default
.BR auto .
.TP
.B buffer
Lines kept for the search.
Default 100000.
.TP
.B ansi
.B strip
or
.BR keep .
Default
.BR strip .
.TP
.B fzf_opts
Extra fzf options.
.TP
.B preview
Whether the preview pane is available.
Default
.BR true .
.TP
.B preview_window
The
.B \-\-preview\-window
option of fzf.
.TP
.B keys.preview_toggle
.TQ
.B keys.accept
The keys that open the preview and that accept a line.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/magenta/
The configuration directory, or
.I ~/.config/magenta/
when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is not set.
It holds
.IR config.toml ,
.IR rules/ ,
and
.IR colorschemes/ .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EDITOR
The editor for the
.B edit
commands.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the configuration directory is.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set and not empty, no colors are written.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed, for example a rule or colorscheme did not pass its check.
.TP
.B 2
The command line is not valid.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.EX
magenta doctor
magenta colorscheme list
magenta colorscheme use mono
magenta config set theme light
magenta rule new myapp
magenta rule check
magenta preview
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mgnt (1)
.PP
Documentation and source: https://github.com/styd/magenta
